===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*terkʷ-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|-}}, from {{der|en|LL.|torsio|torsio, torsionem}}, from {{der|en|la|tortio}}, from {{m|la|torqueō||twist, turn}}. See {{m|en|torture}}, {{m|en|-tort}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈtɔː.ʃən/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The act of [[turn]]ing or twisting, or the state of being twisted; the twisting or [[wrench]]ing of a body by the [[exertion]] of a [[lateral]] [[force]] tending to turn one end or part of it about a [[longitudinal]] [[axis]], while the other is held [[fast]] or turned in the opposite direction.
# {{lb|en|mechanics}} That force with which a thread, wire, or rod of any material, returns, or tends to return, to a state of rest after it has been twisted; [[torsibility]].
# {{lb|en|surgery}} The stopping of [[arterial]] [[haemorrhage]] in certain cases, by [[twist]]ing the cut end of the [[artery]].

